From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Murray <ryan@aurorasilicon.org>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 14:50:31 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 1006/1006] filter-graph: keep the software volume at unity on
 every volume update

When the graph carries the volume on its own controls (capture.volumes
or playback.volumes), impl_set_props() sets softVolumes to 1.0 so the
converter after it does not apply the volume again.  It only did that
when the volume or mute state changed.  An update that repeats the
current values (a desktop re-sending the slider position, an unmute of
a sink that is not muted, a session manager restoring the same volume)
went through with the caller's softVolumes, or, for a mute-only update,
with no softVolumes at all, in which case audioconvert falls back to
the channel volumes.  Either way the converter applied the channel
volume in software on top of the graph's control: the output dropped by
the volume a second time (-31 dB at a 30 % cubic slider, -12 dB at
63 %) on every band, and stayed there until the next real change.

Set the soft volumes to unity (0 when muted) for every Props update
that has a volume or mute property when the graph has volume controls,
and only re-sync the controls when something changed.  Graphs without
volume controls still pass softVolumes on unmodified (#5344).

Add a test that sends a volume, the same volume again (with and
without softVolumes), a mute-only unmute, mute and unmute, and checks
softVolumes/softMute in the props passed on; and that a graph without
volume controls passes softVolumes through.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Ryan Murray <ryan@aurorasilicon.org>
---
 spa/plugins/filter-graph/filter-graph.c |  29 +++-
 test/meson.build                        |   8 +
 test/test-filter-graph-volume.c         | 193 ++++++++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 222 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 test/test-filter-graph-volume.c

diff --git a/spa/plugins/filter-graph/filter-graph.c b/spa/plugins/filter-graph/filter-graph.c
index f111618..88f26d3 100644
--- a/spa/plugins/filter-graph/filter-graph.c
+++ b/spa/plugins/filter-graph/filter-graph.c
@@ -792,7 +792,7 @@ static int impl_set_props(void *object, enum spa_direction direction, const stru
 	float soft_vols[MAX_CHANNELS];
 	uint32_t n_soft_vols = 0;
 	bool soft_mute = false, have_soft_mute = false;
-	bool do_volume = false;
+	bool do_volume = false, have_volume = false;
 
 	spa_pod_dynamic_builder_init(&b, buf, sizeof(buf), 1024);
 	spa_pod_builder_push_object(&b.b, &f[0], SPA_TYPE_OBJECT_Props, SPA_PARAM_Props);
@@ -806,6 +806,7 @@ static int impl_set_props(void *object, enum spa_direction direction, const stru
 		case SPA_PROP_mute:
 		{
 			bool mute;
+			have_volume = true;
 			if (spa_pod_get_bool(&prop->value, &mute) == 0) {
 				if (vol->mute != mute) {
 					vol->mute = mute;
@@ -820,6 +821,7 @@ static int impl_set_props(void *object, enum spa_direction direction, const stru
 			uint32_t i, n_vols;
 			float vols[MAX_CHANNELS];
 
+			have_volume = true;
 			if ((n_vols = spa_pod_copy_array(&prop->value, SPA_TYPE_Float, vols,
 					SPA_N_ELEMENTS(vols))) > 0) {
 				if (vol->n_volumes != n_vols)
@@ -837,10 +839,12 @@ static int impl_set_props(void *object, enum spa_direction direction, const stru
 			break;
 		}
 		case SPA_PROP_softVolumes:
+			have_volume = true;
 			n_soft_vols = spa_pod_copy_array(&prop->value, SPA_TYPE_Float, soft_vols,
 					SPA_N_ELEMENTS(soft_vols));
 			break;
 		case SPA_PROP_softMute:
+			have_volume = true;
 			if (spa_pod_get_bool(&prop->value, &soft_mute) == 0)
 				have_soft_mute = true;
 			break;
@@ -849,16 +853,25 @@ static int impl_set_props(void *object, enum spa_direction direction, const stru
 			break;
 		}
 	}
-	if (do_volume && vol->n_ports != 0) {
-		uint32_t i;
-
-		for (i = 0; i < vol->n_volumes; i++)
-			soft_vols[i] = (vol->mute || vol->volumes[i] == 0.0f) ? 0.0f : 1.0f;
-		n_soft_vols = vol->n_volumes;
+	if (have_volume && vol->n_ports != 0) {
+		/* The graph applies the volume, so the software volume after it
+		 * must stay at unity (or 0 when muted). Do this for every Props
+		 * that carries a volume or mute, also when the values did not
+		 * change: passing the given softVolumes on, or leaving them out
+		 * so that the channelVolumes are used, applies the volume a
+		 * second time in software. */
+		uint32_t i, n = vol->n_volumes > 0 ? vol->n_volumes : n_soft_vols;
+
+		for (i = 0; i < n; i++)
+			soft_vols[i] = (vol->mute ||
+					(i < vol->n_volumes && vol->volumes[i] == 0.0f)) ?
+				0.0f : 1.0f;
+		n_soft_vols = n;
 		soft_mute = vol->mute;
 		have_soft_mute = true;
 
-		sync_volume(graph, vol);
+		if (do_volume)
+			sync_volume(graph, vol);
 	}
 	if (have_soft_mute) {
 		spa_pod_builder_prop(&b.b, SPA_PROP_softMute, 0);
diff --git a/test/meson.build b/test/meson.build
index 625240c..38a6a85 100644
--- a/test/meson.build
+++ b/test/meson.build
@@ -115,6 +115,14 @@ test('test-filter-graph-latency',
     depends: latency_step_plugin
 )
 
+test('test-filter-graph-volume',
+    executable('test-filter-graph-volume',
+               'test-filter-graph-volume.c',
+               include_directories: pwtest_inc,
